    "updated_at": "2021-05-07T15:14:20Z",
    "body": "Can confirm this change in behavior.  Just updated to 0.53.0 and now I have a `0` on my prompt with `threshold=0`.  If I set it to `threshold=1` the output only shows up when there are 2 or more jobs.\r\n\r\nI know Python not Rust, but I looked through `src/modules/jobs.rs` and here is the line that I think needs changed to handle the case where the number of jobs does not show when the threshold is greater than 0 and the number of jobs is equal to the threshold value:\r\n\r\nThis line:\r\n` let module_number = if num_of_jobs > config.threshold || config.threshold == 0 {`\r\n\r\nChange to this:\r\n` let module_number = if num_of_jobs >= config.threshold || config.threshold == 0 {`\r\n\r\nIf I am following the code correctly, this should let it show 1 or more jobs with `threshold=1` or always show the number if `threshold=0`.\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n",
