    "created_at": "2021-06-28T17:32:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-06-28T17:33:54Z",
    "body": "Maybe there should be a param. for \"show number for single job\". Previously, I was using `threshold = 0` for this, but now with that configuration, `+0` is shown for zero jobs, which is needless cruft.\r\n\r\nThe parameter wouldn't make sense in combination with the current behaviour of `threshold = 0` though, since in that case the user would probably always want to see a number.\r\n\r\nPersonally I'd be in favour of just always showing an explicit number instead of having a config. option, but there may be other users who wouldn't like that behaviour for a single job.\r\n\r\nEdit: another option would be to have different params - `$number` and `$number_if_gt_1` or similar.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
