    "updated_at": "2021-06-30T12:38:50Z",
    "body": "See also https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/2830.\r\n\r\nI think the solution for this is:\r\n\r\n* `threshold` should have the semantic of \"at least\", not \"greater than\" - e.g. `1` would mean \"show count when 1 or more jobs\". This would allow showing a number when there are 0 jobs, without having to accept negative numbers for `threshold`. In fact per the above bug, it does this already for `threshold = 0`, but that's special-cased behaviour and contrary to the documentation.\r\n* A new config. parameter for \"show when no jobs\", defaulting to `false` should be added.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
